module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.release_gate_requires_evidence_the_held_population_never_wrote

// THE MIRROR OF guard_precondition_discharged_by_the_route_that_uses_it, filed as its own class on
// quick-newt-573's instruction (2026-11-02) after PR #15640's review 89894 caught it in progress. That
// row is a guard whose premise moved underneath it so it reports PASS forever and the deficit never
// ranks; THIS row is a release rule whose required evidence moved underneath it so it refuses forever
// and the capacity never comes back. Opposite polarity, opposite harm, opposite review behaviour: the
// silently-passing guard looks healthy and is reported; the permanently-refusing release rule looks
// healthy AND is reported as fail-closed good practice, which is why it needs its own rung.

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data release_gate_requires_evidence_the_held_population_never_wrote: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "release_gate_requires_evidence_the_held_population_never_wrote" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "a deploy-time census that reads the revision an instance is running against the evidence each of its release rules demands, and refuses to call that instance converged while a held population could not satisfy the demand"
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a rule that frees a held resource (a capacity seat, a lease, a slot, a grant) is written so that exactly one piece of evidence frees it, and that evidence is written by a component the held population never ran -- an older launcher, a route predating the artifact, a provider that could not obtain the identity the artifact is keyed by, or a store root the population was never placed in. The rule is correct for every holder created after the artifact's writer shipped, so every review of it passes; for the population created BEFORE, the freeing arm is unreachable and the refusal is typed, sourced, and permanent. HARM: the hold never returns to the pool, and nothing in the system calls that a defect, because the refusal is the behaviour the rule was written to have. WHO IS MISLED: the reviewer sees a fail-closed release rule and approves it; the operator sees a full pool with no acquisition that failed; the next placement request gets a refusal with no named way out.",

    "THE POLARITY IS THE POINT, AND IT IS WHY THIS IS NOT the same class as guard_precondition_discharged_by_the_route_that_uses_it. That row: a guard still executing exactly as designed, whose driver condition stopped being reachable, so it reports PASS forever and the deficit never ranks -- discovered by a witness catching the guard's answer being treated as evidence. THIS row: a release rule still executing exactly as designed, whose freeing evidence stopped being reachable, so it reports REFUSE forever and the capacity never ranks -- discovered only when a seat is missed by a deadline, because nothing treats a refusal as a defect. The same underlying event (a change elsewhere moved the premise) produces opposite verdicts and opposite review behaviour: PASS-forever is invisible because it is reported as health, REFUSE-forever is invisible because it is reported as rigour. A row that covered only one polarity would let the other be filed against it.",

    "MEASURED RECEIPT (srv1, read-only, 2026-11-01, bright-moth-475's report to quick-newt-573 msg_972744b7 and this lane's own reads): /opt/gunbc/compute/capacity/heads/session-memory-srv1.92 carries 47 acquisitions and 45 releases -- two 22 GiB session-memory terms open with no holder. gunbc-attempt-debt-exclusion-frontier-excludes-nothing-6ea61c671002a6d4.service (acquired 1793161645, 2026-10-28T04:27:25Z): the attempt slot is state Launching at generation 2 in the instance's session-attempts store, systemctl reports LoadState=not-found with empty InvocationID, ExecMainStartTimestamp and UnitFileState, and the attempt-exit spool holds only an UNDECODABLE entry in refused/ whose systemd stop-hook variables were never substituted (written 1793168222, owned briansrls rather than the worker account). The lifecycle reader could therefore return only unknown, and the unknown arm keeps the charge. gunbc-attempt-v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority-25de491353dd507f.service (acquired 1792001070, 2026-10-14T18:04:30Z): its slot exists only in the pre-re-root store ~/.local/share/gunbc-dashboard-instances/codex-provider-feedback-v0/attempt-state/session-attempts, and the settle pass enumerates the current instance's slots root, so no pass could ever see the slot the release would be read from. Consequence on the live system: the lab placement for codex-provider-feedback-v0 refused with 503 no_placement_grant at 22 GiB, while compute-memory-srv1 sat balanced at 154/154.",

    "WHY NOBODY WEAKENED ANYTHING -- this is the property that makes the class cheap to miss. The rule is STRENGTHENED, never loosened: a release that used to fire on a bare unit absence is made to require the unit's own exit record, so a not-found reading can no longer free a seat that is in fact running. Every reviewer approves that; the operator's standing demands it (no release on an age or a name, holder death bound to manager, boot, and invocation). The unexamined part is the POPULATION: every holder already running when the strengthening lands launched before the record existed, and every holder whose launcher cannot reach the artifact's key can never write one. The strengthening is what turns a leak that time could clear into a leak that nothing can clear, and it arrives dressed as the fix.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE (the next site, spotted before it ships): take any rule whose freeing arm is gated on an artifact's existence, a record's decodability, or a witness the holder itself must supply, and ask two questions of the CURRENT held population, not of the rule -- (1) which of these holders was created before the component that writes this evidence existed, or by a route that cannot obtain the identity the evidence is keyed by? (2) what frees THOSE, by name? If the answer is 'nothing, they stay charged', the rule is this class. A release rule is not complete when its freeing arm is sound; it is complete when every reachable state of the population has a named path out.",

    "NOT THIS CLASS, three boundaries. (a) A refusal that is BOUNDED -- retried under a stated budget, or escalated with a named interim fallback and a dissolution trigger -- is section 5's legitimate fail-closed, not this; the class is the refusal with neither an exit nor a deadline. (b) A missing artifact caused by a bug in the writer is the writer's defect and belongs to the writer (the fix for the srv1 spool entry was to make the unexpanded name unwritable at the spool put, not to reinterpret the entry); this class begins where the writer is correct and simply never existed for the holder. (c) A population left behind by a moved store root is a migration defect with its own remedy (carry the slots forward, once, keyed by lease reference and slot generation, and then let the old root hold nothing); what makes it an instance of THIS class is leaving the settle pass enumerating historical roots as a second authority instead of migrating.",

    "CURRENT RUNG: mitigatable, and the mitigation has a shape rather than a mood -- every refusal arm of a release rule carries (i) the reason it refused, (ii) the name of an alternate path that does free the holder, and (iii) the dissolution trigger of that alternate, so a reviewer can see the population with no path out from the refusal itself. WHO HAS THAT SHAPE: the #15640 CANDIDATE (head c6ae064696c6, UNMERGED), which makes the seat's stop-hook record one witness and the provider's own recorded wait beside a kernel-confirmed-empty cgroup the named alternate, with each refusal arm stating when it stops applying. That candidate mitigation is NOT implemented by this row, is NOT established as deployed anywhere, and is NOT the behaviour of this main-based tree: here unit_termination_unconfirmed still frees on a bare absence and unit_lifecycle_unpopulated still terminates on one. The rung is claimed for the SHAPE a mitigation must have, not for any tree's current code. CEILING: mechanically preventable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER (a capability, not an artifact): the deploy-time census named in the rung -- the fleet refuses to report an instance converged while the revision it runs cannot satisfy the evidence its own release rules demand, which makes the writer-gap population impossible to deploy rather than impossible to notice.",

    "OPERATOR STANDING on the measured instance (quick-newt-573, 2026-11-01, restated 2026-11-02): the two srv1 seats return through the MODELED settlement only. No hand edit of the ledger or the spool, no release on age, and running the settle or the carry on srv1 is a mutation needing its own explicit authorization with fresh readings taken after srv1 reopens. Filing this row is not that authorization, and the row claims no release: the releases land when the settlement rules that admit them are deployed and run.",

    "NAMED SITES, so the census can count rather than guess. SITE 1 -- the compute seat termination fold (gunbc.compute.work_provider_local unit_termination_unconfirmed) and its recovery twin (unit_lifecycle_unpopulated), OBSERVED IN THIS main-based TREE: a seat whose unit is absent from the user manager is freed on the BARE absence -- the termination fold yields UnitAbsentAuthoritatively and the recovery fold yields UnitTerminatedCauseUnknown, both from a LoadState reading alone. That is the neighbouring error this class sits next to: a name a manager no longer lists is read as proof of death. The #15640 candidate closes it by demanding evidence of how the seat ended, and that very demand is what opens THIS class for the population that cannot supply the evidence -- a seat launched before the stop-hook existed, or by a provider that could not read the uid the record is keyed by, writes nothing, and would then have no path out unless the candidate's recorded-wait alternate ships with it. So the site is open in both directions depending on which rule is running: today a seat can be freed on a reading that is not death proof; under the candidate a pre-existing seat can be kept forever. Neither direction is acceptable, and the row exists to make whoever writes the next version of this rule check the population, not just the rule. SITE 2 -- the session placement settle pass (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement session_placement_settle_pass through session_worker_unit_lifecycle_for_instance): a Launching slot whose unit reports not-found keeps its charge while the holder-death reading cannot be bound to manager, boot, and acquisition instant, which is correct, and keeps it forever if no alternate is named, which is this class. SITE 3 -- the exit spool decoder (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool): an entry whose stop-hook variables were never substituted is evidence about its WRITER, never about its holder; reading it either way is the neighbouring error, and the writer-side fix is what stops the artifact being written at all.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.work_provider_local", decl_name: "unit_termination_unconfirmed"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.work_provider_local", decl_name: "unit_lifecycle_unpopulated"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement", decl_name: "session_worker_unit_lifecycle_for_instance"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement", decl_name: "session_placement_settle_pass"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness", decl_name: "unit_reboot_holder_liveness"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool", decl_name: "AttemptExitRecord"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool", decl_name: "AttemptExitEntryDecode"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "attempt_slots_carry_for_instance"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.resource_release_law", decl_name: "ReleaseLaw"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.guard_precondition_discharged_by_the_route_that_uses_it", decl_name: "guard_precondition_discharged_by_the_route_that_uses_it"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.hold_recovered_by_age_not_observed_holder_death", decl_name: "hold_recovered_by_age_not_observed_holder_death"),
  ],
}
